      "subUnits": [
        "1-sas-squadron"
      ],
      "report": "YS546787: A LRRP FROM 1 ATF CONTACTED 7 VC AT LOCSTATED. RES 7 VC KIA (BC), AND THREE WPNS CAPTURED. THEVC WERE DRESSED IN MIXED DRESS AND CARRYING A LARGE AMOUNT OFFOOD. THERE WERE FIVE MALES AND TWO FEMALES. THE WPNSCAPTURED WERE 1 X CHICOM 7.62 RIFLE, 1 X MI944 CARBINE, 1 USM1 .30 RIFLE, THERE WERE NO DOCS.\n\nGlover",
      "archivalSource": "Intsum, AWM95 1/4/74.pdf p116; AWM 569/R4/77; Horner SAS pg230; AWM95 7-10-12.pdf 1 SAS pg124"
    },
    {
      "id": 1090,
      "url": "/battlemap?incident=1090",
      "dtg": "1968-03-18T23:10:00",
      "why": [
        "significant"
      ],
      "role": "led",
      "ledBy": null,
      "operation": "LRRP",
      "task": "Ambush",
      "gridRef": "YS355864",
      "friendlyForce": 5,
      "enemyForce": 30,
      "friendlyKilled": 0,
      "friendlyWounded": 0,
      "enemyKilled": 21,
      "enemyWounded": 0,
      "units": [
        "13 Patrol, 2 SAS Squadron, Special Air Service Regiment"
      ],
      "subUnits": [
        "2-sas-squadron"
      ],
      "report": "YS358864: AT THE LOC STATED A BEEHIVE AND CLAYMORE MINESYSTEM PLACED BY A 1ATF LRRP DETONATED UNDER A TRACTOR ANDTRAILER CARRYING AMMUNITION, WEAPONS AND PERSONAL EQUIPMENT.RESULTS; 15 VC KIA (BC), 1X75MM RR AND ONE 75MM RR ROUND WERECAPTURED. THE TRACTOR AND TRAILER WERE DESTROYED. THERE WERESIX OR EIGHT MORE RR ROUNDS IN THE AREA AS WELL AS AN UNDETERMINEDAMOUNT OF SA AMMUNITION AND PERSONAL EQUIPMENT. LFT ENGAGED THEAREA CAUSING TWO SECONDARY EXPLOSIONS. VR AIRCRAFT RECEIVEDGROUND FIRE TWICE FROM THE AREA. THE PATROL WAS EXTRACTED AFTERTHE INCIDENT. AN A-S WAS ALSO CONDUCTED ON THE AREA WITH NO BDA.\n\nCashmores SAS patrol used explosives and claymores. Enemy defector from same unit which ran tractor said that 21 enemy died in explosions.",
      "archivalSource": "Horner SAS, pg8-15; AWM95 7-11-1.pdf 2 SAS pg156; Intsum AWM95 1/4/91.pdf p119;"
    },
    {
      "id": 1164,
      "url": "/battlemap?incident=1164",
      "dtg": "1968-04-17T08:45:00",
      "why": [
        "typical:Ambush"
      ],
      "role": "led",
      "ledBy": null,
      "operation": "LRRP",
      "task": "Ambush",
      "gridRef": "YS349716",
      "friendlyForce": 10,
      "enemyForce": 8,
      "friendlyKilled": 0,
      "friendlyWounded": 0,
      "enemyKilled": 7,
      "enemyWounded": 0,
      "units": [
        "35 Patrol, 2 SAS Squadron, Special Air Service Regiment"
      ],
      "subUnits": [
        "2-sas-squadron"
      ],
      "report": "YS349716: AT THE LOC STATED, A 1 ATF LRRP CON 8 VC WHO WALKED INTO A AMBUSH SET BY THE LRRP. RES; 6 VC KIA (BC) AND 1 VC KIA(POSS). THERE WERE ALSO 12 VC IN THE AREA WHO DID NOT ENTER THE AMBUSH ZONE. THE AREA WAS ENGAGED BY ARTY WITH UNKNOWN RES.\n\nThe ptl was waiting in ambush when a party of 8 enemy entered in two groups of 4. The 2ic initiated the ambush from the centre with 3 claymores. He wiped out the second enemy group of 4. The left flank fired another claymore at members of the first enemy group, killing 1 and possibly killing another. The first enemy went to ground and opened fire with an LMG. The 4th enemy was engaged by SA and fell dead. The first enemy was engaged with SA and 1 M26 and fell silent. As the ptl withdrew they were fired on from the left flank by 4 enemy with SA and an LMG. The patrol was extracted.",
      "archivalSource": "Intsum, AWM95 1/4/94 pt3.pdf p104; AWM95 7-11-2.pdf 2 SAS pg130"
    },
    {
      "id": 1183,
      "url": "/battlemap?incident=1183",
      "dtg": "1968-04-26T10:00:00",
      "why": [
        "typical:Patrol"
      ],
      "role": "led",
      "ledBy": null,
      "operation": "LRRP",
      "task": "Patrol",
      "gridRef": "YS279807",
      "friendlyForce": 14,
      "enemyForce": 4,
      "friendlyKilled": 0,
      "friendlyWounded": 0,
      "enemyKilled": 4,
      "enemyWounded": 0,
      "units": [
        "11 Patrol, 2 SAS Squadron, Special Air Service Regiment",
        "25 Patrol, 2 SAS Squadron, Special Air Service Regiment",
        "31 Patrol, 2 SAS Squadron, Special Air Service Regiment"
      ],
      "subUnits": [
        "2-sas-squadron"
      ],
      "report": "YT278805: AT LOC STATED, A 1 ATF LRRP CONTACTED7 VC. RESULTS 4 VC KIA (BC) \n\nScutts SAS patrol of 19 men was sent to ambush the recently abandoned FSB Dyke. 3 enemy were seen on 26/4 but were not in a good position for the patrol to ambush. Scutts sent a 5 man patrol to come at the enemy from another direction. Meanwhile he moved the rest of his ptl in another direction. After 120m they saw another group of 4 enemy at 7m range. The OC  fired on the first 2 with his M16 and with M79, killing both. The 3rd enemy was hit by 2 burst of 30rds from a FN and killed. The 4th was hit by 20rds of M16 fire and an M79 gren and dropped dead. The area of the contact was then engaged with further SA and M79. The other enemy party was then attacked (see next contact for same patrol same time).",
      "archivalSource": "Horner SAS, pg254-5; AWM95 7-11-2.pdf 2 SAS pg160;"
    },
